#!/command/with-contenv sh
# The page operator (plan §3.1; src/operator/), as pb-operator: Chrome's
# only way out, its control through the holder, the engine's RPC. It stands
# with the exit closed until the engine starts the page.
#
# The page's RPC token is the container's secret, root's alone: it is copied
# into the operator's own directory before the operator starts. No token, no
# operator — the service fails and the container is not healthy. The API's
# token of the login form (PR 15) goes the same way; a container made
# without one runs with the form refused.
set -eu
umask 077
[ -s /run/secrets/rpc_token ] || { echo "operator: no RPC token in /run/secrets/rpc_token" >&2; exit 1; }
install -o pb-operator -g pb-operator -m 400 /run/secrets/rpc_token /run/pb/operator/rpc_token
if [ -s /run/secrets/api_token ]; then
  install -o pb-operator -g pb-operator -m 400 /run/secrets/api_token /run/pb/operator/api_token
else
  rm -f /run/pb/operator/api_token
fi
exec env -i HOME=/home/pb-operator PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin \
  PB_OPERATOR_VERSION="${PB_OPERATOR_VERSION:-dev}" PB_RPC_HOST="${PB_CONTROL_IP:-0.0.0.0}" \
  /command/s6-setuidgid pb-operator node --no-warnings /opt/page-browser/src/operator/main.ts
